From: =?UTF-8?q?Enrico=20B=C3=BChler?= <enrico.buehler@unom.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:19:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(host/mgmt): answer the plane bootstrap over plain
 HTTP

A packaged TV page runs from file://, and nothing there completes a TLS
connection to the host's self-signed certificate: not fetch, not an img,
and nobody clicks through a warning on a TV. Without the plane's
certificate hash the page cannot dial the plane, so it had no way in.

The management port now tells a TLS peer from a plain one by the first
byte (0x16 opens a ClientHello; no HTTP method does) and answers plain
HTTP with one route, GET /api/v1/webtransport, behind the CORS layer,
only while the browser plane runs. It carries what HTTPS already serves
to anyone: a hash any peer learns by connecting, and an attestation a
paired page checks against the identity it pinned. Every other path is
404. A host without the plane listens exactly as before.
